text.section:
Any district created under the provisions of this chapter may be abolished by resolutions passed by each board of supervisors upon the joint petition of the commission and the owners of at least 51 percent of the land area located within the district in each county. A joint petition:

May state whether the purposes for which the district was formed substantially have been achieved;


May state that all obligations theretofore incurred by the district have been fully paid;


May describe the benefits which can be expected from the abolition of the district; and


Shall request each board of supervisors to abolish the district.
